  "review": {
    "review": "The hero remained alive, but the planner stopped after retaining a lightning threat from a defeated DM-100. D3400, log lines 9727–9728, records the frost zap; D3401, line 9730, shows one charge consumed, one turn elapsed, six XP through a level-up, and no remaining DM-100. Arcane Vision tracks a struck survivor. The accepted-attack receipt chain in tools/combat_observation.py supported missile, prismatic and disintegration receipts, but not this chilled frost target beside a chest. The remembered lane then preempted progress at tools/policy_nodes.py:126–127. Last-resort healing did not resolve it; D3402 ended with 70/70 HP. A focused candidate adds a narrowly validated frost receipt and a new regression, preserving hazard admission, mandatory pickups, terminal exhaustion and honest collection accounting. The new test fails on the original policy and passes on the candidate; the full suite passes 2465 tests with four skipped. An isolated reconstruction using original public snapshots matched both recorded attack inputs and confirmed the receipt difference; original full-run memory was not recovered. This establishes removal of the stale veto, not a successful next action, reward collection or improved survival.",
    "learnings": "A tracked frost kill can award XP without a rendered defeat message. Validate the consumed charge, clear ray, one-turn six-XP receipt and absence of a tracked survivor before retiring only that matching threat. Chilled targets remain hittable; frozen targets do not establish this receipt. Retirement must not grant loot or floor-clear credit."
  },
